=== systemd-creds ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Display and Process Credentials.


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  systemd-creds [OPTIONS...] COMMAND ...


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  COMMAND


FLAGS (21) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-h, --help                   Show this help
    --version                Show package version
    --no-pager               Do not pipe output into a pager
    --no-legend              Do not show the headers and footers
    --json pretty|short|off  Generate JSON output
    --system                 Show credentials passed to system
    --transcode base64|unbase64|hex|unhex Transcode credential data
    --newline auto|yes|no    Suffix output with newline
-p, --pretty                 Output as SetCredentialEncrypted= line
    --name NAME              Override filename included in encrypted
                             credential
    --timestamp TIME         Include specified timestamp in encrypted
                             credential
    --not-after TIME         Include specified invalidation time in
                             encrypted credential
    --with-key host|tpm2|host+tpm2|tpm2-absent|auto|auto-initrd Which keys
                             to encrypt with
-H                           Shortcut for --with-key=host
-T                           Shortcut for --with-key=tpm2
    --tpm2-device PATH       Pick TPM2 device
    --tpm2-pcrs PCR1+PCR2+PCR3+… Specify TPM2 PCRs to seal against (fixed
                             hash)
    --tpm2-public-key PATH   Specify PEM certificate to seal against
    --tpm2-public-key-pcrs PCR1+PCR2+PCR3+… Specify TPM2 PCRs to seal
                             against (public key)
    --tpm2-signature PATH    Specify signature for public key PCR policy
-q, --quiet                  Suppress output for 'has-tpm2' verb

=== systemd-creds list ===
Show installed and available versions

=== systemd-creds cat ===
Show specified credentials


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  cat CREDENTIAL...

=== systemd-creds setup ===
Generate credentials host key, if not existing yet

=== systemd-creds encrypt ===
Encrypt plaintext credential file and write to ciphertext credential file


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  encrypt INPUT OUTPUT

=== systemd-creds decrypt ===
Decrypt ciphertext credential file and write to plaintext credential file


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  decrypt INPUT [OUTPUT]

=== systemd-creds has-tpm2 ===
Report whether TPM2 support is available
